Module 1: RF Front End (RF_IN to PREAMP)

Purpose:
- Receive external RF input (SMA/BNC), maintain 50Ω transmission, provide fixed attenuation option, DC-block for AC coupling, and transient protection.

Schematic description (to import into CAD manually):
- J1 SMA (RF_IN_RAW) center -> PAD_20dB (Mini-Circuits PAD-20) input -> PAD_OUT -> C_DC_BLOCK (1nF RF-grade, series) -> NET RF_AFTER_DC
- Option: For DC mode, solder jumper JP_DC_SHORT to bypass C_DC_BLOCK (NET RF_AFTER_DC = RF_IN_ATT direct)
- TVS: D1 low-capacitance TVS from NET RF_AFTER_DC to GND (choose low C ~0.5pF-5pF), series Rlimit=2Ω placed upstream if needed for surge dissipation.
- RF_OUT: NET RF_PREAMP_IN (50Ω) routed with controlled-impedance microstrip to next stage.

Components (suggested):
- SMA connector J1, 50Ω
- Attenuator: Mini-Circuits PAD-20 (20dB) or pad network (R values per design)
- DC block: Murata RF MLCC 1nF, NP0/COG, high SRF
- TVS: Low-capacitance TVS (e.g., SMBJ or vendor low-C family)
- Jumpers: JP_DC_SHORT for AC/DC selection

Layout notes:
- Keep SMA->pad->DC-block short; maintain 50Ω trace.
- Ground plane under microstrip, via stitching every quarter wavelength at 100 MHz not critical but keep consistent.

Verification:
- Use VNA to measure S11 and S21 of this section; expected insertion loss ~ PAD spec, return loss <-12dB
